# The reason a blind external costs far more than its own bytes.
#
# `double-quoted-string.php` shows php cannot lex `"x"`. This shows what
# happens NEXT, and it is the finding this lane exists for. Outliner's forest
# over these 70 bytes:
#
#   php_tag       [0, 5)
#   variable_name [6, 8)
#   name          [7, 8)
#   program      [13, 70)
#   text         [13, 70)
#
# `text` is php's node for inline HTML outside `<?php`. Both function
# definitions - 57 of the file's 70 bytes - are read as raw HTML text. And
# because `program [13, 70)` is a top-level node WITH a child, the board's
# `built` counts every one of those 57 bytes as read.
#
# So the recovery does not orphan the remainder, it claims it. A blind
# external costs its own bytes plus everything downstream of it, and the
# downstream bytes score as a WIN. In `Str.php` the same route turns the
# 40,995 bytes after byte 26,850 into one `text` node, which is 32,615 of the
# corpus's 33,634 regrouped bytes - 97% of the whole finding, from one
# unlexable token.
#
# The claims are tree-sitter's answer. They fail today.
roots 1
mends 0
lacks text
holds function_definition
